You are building FounderOS — an AI startup validation platform for founders.

PROJECT STACK:
- Next.js with App Router
- Tailwind CSS
- Groq API (model: llama-3.3-70b-versatile)
- API key stored in .env.local as GROQ_API_KEY

DESIGN RULES — ALWAYS follow these:
- Background: #0c0c0f (dark)
- Accent color: #ff4d2e (orange-red)
- Headings font: Syne (Google Fonts)
- Body font: DM Sans (Google Fonts)
- All UI must be mobile friendly
- Dark cards with subtle borders (#1e1e2a)
- No purple gradients ever

WHAT THIS APP DOES:
- User types a startup idea
- Clicks "Analyze My Idea"
- Groq API analyzes it and returns JSON
- Results shown in styled cards:
  Market Demand Score, Top 5 Competitors,
  3 Biggest Risks, 3 Market Opportunities,
  Overall Viability Score, Advisor Summary

BUILD ORDER — when I ask for new features, do them in this order:
1. Landing page + idea input (DONE)
2. Razorpay payment (₹499) before showing report
3. User login with Google (Firebase Auth)
4. Save past reports to user account
5. AI Advisor chat (remembers your idea history)
6. Financial model generator
7. Pitch deck generator

IMPORTANT RULES:
- NEVER break features that are already working
- NEVER add features I didn't ask for
- NEVER put API keys in the code — always use .env.local
- Keep code clean and simple
- If something isn't working, fix the simplest thing first
- Always tell me what you changed and why